{% comment %}
  Which desktop panel layout a top-level mega menu item uses.

  Accepts:
  - parent: {String} the top-level item's title, e.g. "Engagement"

  Outputs:
  - "links" - the text-only panel: named options in columns, no picture tiles
    ('header-menu-drawer-links')
  - nothing  - the default tabs-and-tiles panel ('header-menu-drawer-panel')

  A menu listed here still needs its groups in 'menu-static-groups' so the header counts it
  as drawer-eligible, and its lists still come from 'menu-static-items'; only the way they
  are drawn changes.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign parent_key = parent | handle

  comment
    Every drawer menu is drawn this way now: the panels differ only in the columns they list,
    which 'header-menu-drawer-links' sets per menu. The tabs-and-tiles panel below it in
    'header-menu-drawer-panel' is what a menu falls back to when it isn't named here.
  endcomment
  case parent_key
    when 'engagement' or 'wedding' or 'diamonds' or 'jewellery' or 'jewelry'
      echo 'links'
  endcase
-%}
